{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reshaped the observed response `y` from an `N` by `T` matrix into a length `N * T` vector in row-major order: `y[(n - 1) * T + t]` equals the original matrix entry `y[n, t]`. The nested elementwise likelihood was replaced by one vectorized built-in sampling statement on the plain top-level protected variable `y`, outside loops. The linear predictors are computed deterministically in the same row-major order after all parameter priors, preserving the original joint density.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  int<lower=1> T;
  vector[T] time;
  vector[N * T] y;
}
parameters {
  real mu_alpha;
  real mu_beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma_alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma_beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
  vector[N] alpha_raw;
  vector[N] beta_raw;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[N] alpha = mu_alpha + sigma_alpha * alpha_raw;
  vector[N] beta = mu_beta + sigma_beta * beta_raw;
}
model {
  vector[N * T] mu_y;

  mu_alpha ~ normal(50, 20);
  mu_beta ~ normal(7, 5);
  sigma_alpha ~ normal(0, 10);
  sigma_beta ~ normal(0, 5);
  sigma_y ~ normal(0, 5);
  alpha_raw ~ normal(0, 1);
  beta_raw ~ normal(0, 1);

  for (n in 1 : N) {
    for (t in 1 : T) {
      mu_y[(n - 1) * T + t] = alpha[n] + beta[n] * time[t];
    }
  }
  y ~ normal(mu_y, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":5,"T":3,"time":[1.0,2.0,3.0],"y":[5.0,5.0,3.0,5.0,3.0,5.0,2.0,5.0,5.0,3.0,5.0,4.0,5.0,5.0,5.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
